Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: SteerWiFiBackhaul() on a shared channel number takes the band of the station's radio

0249 sends a modelled target's own operating class and derives an unmodelled target's from
Channel when that number belongs to one band only. 2.4 GHz 1, 5, 9, 13 and 5 GHz 149-177 are 6 GHz
channel numbers too, so a target outside the model on one of them was refused. On a gateway with
two-radio pods (12 October) that refused every steer of a pod back to the gateway's pod-backhaul
BSS on 149: that
BSS is outside EasyMesh by design (its agent keeps the pod-backhaul SSID out), so it is never
modelled, and the Data Elements method takes TargetBSS, Channel and TimeOut, no class (from the
implementation; no OperatingClass input in the Data Elements definition as far as known).

The station that moves decides now: the device's backhaul-STA row the method already uses names
its radio, and the classes that radio's AP Radio Basic Capabilities advertised (the model's
capability rows for its RUID) give the bands it can operate. A shared number takes the 20 MHz class
of the one such band that has it (Annex E, as 0249). A radio advertising none of them, or more than
one (a 5 and 6 GHz radio on 149), or no capability at all, is still refused rather than guessed. A
modelled target and an unshared number are unchanged. gen/tests/
controller-steer-backhaul-station-band-test.py reproduces the refusal with --expect-refused on a
source without this patch.

Platform-independent (the method's native path is the lab's own); not for upstream on its own.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [completes the lab's native SteerWiFiBackhaul() path]

diff --git a/src/ctrl/dm_easy_mesh_ctrl.cpp b/src/ctrl/dm_easy_mesh_ctrl.cpp
index 6d014d9f..a773e072 100644
--- a/src/ctrl/dm_easy_mesh_ctrl.cpp
+++ b/src/ctrl/dm_easy_mesh_ctrl.cpp
@@ -711,6 +711,45 @@ static unsigned char backhaul_op_class_of_channel(int channel)
     return 131;
 }
 
+/* The 20 MHz operating class of a channel number in the one band the moving radio can operate that
+ * has this number. The radio's bands are those of the classes its AP Radio Basic
+ * Capabilities advertised (the model's capability rows for its RUID): 2.4 GHz 81-84, 5 GHz 115-130,
+ * 6 GHz 131-137. For a number several bands use (2.4 GHz 1, 5, 9, 13 and 5 GHz 149-177 are 6 GHz
+ * numbers too) the backhaul STA's own radio decides; 0 when it advertises none of the bands with
+ * this number, or more than one, or no class at all. */
+static unsigned char backhaul_op_class_for_radio(dm_easy_mesh_t *model, const mac_address_t ruid, int channel)
+{
+    bool has_24 = false, has_5 = false, has_6 = false;
+    {
+        std::lock_guard<std::recursive_mutex> topology_lock(g_network_topology_mutex);
+        for (unsigned int o = 0; o < model->m_num_opclass && o < EM_MAX_OPCLASS; o++) {
+            const em_op_class_info_t *op = model->get_op_class_info(o);
+            if (op->id.type != em_op_class_type_capability ||
+                    memcmp(op->id.ruid, ruid, sizeof(mac_address_t)) != 0) {
+                continue;
+            }
+            has_24 = has_24 || (op->op_class >= 81 && op->op_class <= 84);
+            has_5 = has_5 || (op->op_class >= 115 && op->op_class <= 130);
+            has_6 = has_6 || (op->op_class >= 131 && op->op_class <= 137);
+        }
+    }
+    const bool band_24 = has_24 && channel >= 1 && channel <= 14;
+    const bool band_5 = has_5 && ((channel >= 36 && channel <= 64 && channel % 4 == 0) ||
+        (channel >= 100 && channel <= 144 && channel % 4 == 0) ||
+        (channel >= 149 && channel <= 177 && channel % 4 == 1));
+    const bool band_6 = has_6 && channel >= 1 && channel <= 233 && channel % 4 == 1;
+    if (static_cast<int>(band_24) + static_cast<int>(band_5) + static_cast<int>(band_6) != 1) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    if (band_24) {
+        return channel == 14 ? 82 : 81;
+    }
+    if (band_5) {
+        return channel <= 48 ? 115 : channel <= 64 ? 118 : channel <= 144 ? 121 : 125;
+    }
+    return 131;
+}
+
 bus_error_t em_ctrl_t::cmd_steerwifibh(const char *method_name, const bus_data_prop_t *input_params, bus_data_prop_t **output_params, void *async_handle)
 {
     (void)async_handle;
@@ -950,9 +989,10 @@ invalid:
         requested.request.target.assign(reinterpret_cast<const char *>(target_mac), sizeof(mac_address_t));
         /* The request carries the operating class and channel on which the target beacons
          * (EasyMesh 17.2.32): the model's for a target it holds, and a Channel given with it
-         * must be that one; else derived from Channel, when that number names one band. An
-         * unknown target without a Channel, or on a number several bands use, is refused
-         * rather than guessed. */
+         * must be that one; else derived from Channel, when that number names one band, or
+         * one band of those the moving station's own radio advertised (a gateway's
+         * pod-backhaul BSS, outside the model, on 149). An unknown target without a Channel,
+         * or on a number its radio's bands share, is refused rather than guessed. */
         unsigned char op_class = 0, op_channel = 0;
         if (backhaul_target_operation(dm_ctrl, target_mac, &op_class, &op_channel)) {
             if (channel > 0 && channel != op_channel) {
@@ -965,10 +1005,13 @@ invalid:
             }
         } else {
             op_class = backhaul_op_class_of_channel(channel);
+            if (op_class == 0) {
+                op_class = backhaul_op_class_for_radio(dm, bsta->ruid.mac, channel);
+            }
             op_channel = static_cast<unsigned char>(op_class != 0 ? channel : 0);
             if (op_class == 0) {
-                em_printfout("SteerWiFiBackhaul(): TargetBSS %s is not modelled and Channel %d names no single band",
-                    target, channel);
+                em_printfout("SteerWiFiBackhaul(): TargetBSS %s is not modelled and Channel %d names no single band "
+                    "its backhaul STA's radio operates", target, channel);
                 if (output_params) {
                     *output_params = tr_181_t::tr181_set_status_output_prop("Failure");
                 }
